<title>GERMANY: Oil World sees 4.3 mln T Russia 1997 oilseeds crop.</title>
<headline>Oil World sees 4.3 mln T Russia 1997 oilseeds crop.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian oilseeds crop in 1997 may rise to 4.3 million tonnes after 3.3 million tonnes last year, the independent newsletter Oil World said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Citing the Russian farm ministry, it broke down the 1996 figure into 2.8 million tonnes of sunseed, 130,000 tonnes of rapeseed and 350,000 tonnes of soybeans, rounded.</p>
<p>Spring crop plantings this year had been expanded and the negative effects of wet and cool climatic conditions were being overcome, Oil World said.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
